    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The number of distinct Hamilton cycles of a complete graph with <i>n</i> vertices is <span data-math=\"\\left( {n - 1} \\right)\"></span>!.</p>\n<p>Since half of those cycles are the reverse of the others, there are only <span data-math=\"\\frac{{\\left( {n - 1} \\right)!}}{2}\"></span> distinct weighted cycles.</p>\n"
    },
    {
